{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q186600","formula":"C₈H₂₀Sn","hill":"C8H20Sn","elements":["H","C","Sn"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":20.0,"Sn":1.0},"names":{"en":"Tetraethyltin","ru":"Тетраэтилолово"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tetraethyltin or tetraethyl tin is a chemical compound with the formula (CH3CH2)4Sn, that is, a tin atom attached to four ethyl groups. It is an important example of an organotin compound, often abbreviated as TET. Tetraethyltin is a colourless flammable liquid, soluble in diethyl ether and insoluble in water, that freezes at −112 °C and boils at 181 °C. It is used in the electronics industry. Tetraethyltin can be obtained by reacting ethylmagnesium bromide with tin(IV) chloride: SnCl4 + 4 CH3CH2MgBr → (CH3CH2)4Sn + 4 MgBrCl The same reaction can be used to obtain tetra-n-propyltin and tetra-n-butyltin.","ru":"Тетраэтилолово — оловоорганическое соединение, чрезвычайно ядовитая бесцветная жидкость с резким запахом, нерастворимая в воде, растворимая в органических растворителях."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":11704,"mass":234.95,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC[Sn](CC)(CC)CC","inchikey":"RWWNQEOPUOCKGR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"tetraethylstannane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"11704","atoms":29,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.473,"y":-2.6,"z":-0.476,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.016,"y":-1.754,"z":0.701,"el":"C"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Sn"},{"x":0.727,"y":1.122,"z":1.678,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.437,"y":1.601,"z":2.53,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.362,"y":1.207,"z":-1.136,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.679,"y":2.491,"z":-1.577,"el":"C"},{"x":1.651,"y":-0.574,"z":-1.243,"el":"C"},{"x":2.589,"y":-1.492,"z":-0.476,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.0,"y":-3.504,"z":-0.105,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.167,"y":-2.016,"z":-1.117,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.596,"y":-2.917,"z":-1.079,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.323,"y